# Project specific
# NOTE: must be `outputs/*`, not `outputs/`. Git cannot re-include a file
# once its parent directory is excluded, so with `outputs/` every `!` rule
# below was silently dead — which is why no results_summary_*.json ever
# reached the repo despite the exception.
outputs/*
!outputs/mailed_manifest_*.json
!outputs/results_summary_*.json
!outputs/telegram_manifest_*.json
# Accumulated match outcomes — the only durable record of settled results.
# Without this exception it stayed on the CI runner and was lost every run,
# which made the real-data backtest impossible.
!outputs/result_store.json
# settled_*.json is NOT tracked: it is derived from result_store.json by
# export_settled.py and regenerates in seconds. Committed once at 79 MB, which
# GitHub warns about and which buys nothing — result_store.json is the durable
# record, this is a view of it.
!outputs/scoring_calibration.json
!outputs/tennis_calibration.json
# The Dropping Odds workflow commits these; without the exception its
# `git add` was a silent no-op.
!outputs/oddssafari_dropping_*.json
# The website reads this to show a verdict next to each price move. Without the
# exception the nightly rebuild ran, `git add` was silently skipped, and the
# site kept serving whatever model the last manual commit carried.
!outputs/dropping_odds_model.json
# Which "worth it" moves were already mailed today. Runners are ephemeral, so
# without this every window would resend the morning's events.
!outputs/dropping_worth_sent_*.json
# Odds history: the per-run snapshot of every market's price. Runners are
# ephemeral, so this has to live in the repo — otherwise every run would look
# like the first one and could never report a change since the last analysis.
!outputs/oddssafari_odds_history_*.json
# TOP rules (tools/top_rules.py, weekly top_rules.yml) – read by top_picks.
!outputs/top_rules.json
!outputs/top_rules_report.*
# Team history index (tools/build_team_index.py, check_results.yml) – read by /api/teams.
!outputs/team_index/
!outputs/team_aliases.json
!outputs/media_cache.json
*.log
scraper_log.txt
email_config.py
app_integration_config.json
gemini_config.py
groq_config.py

# Chrome driver logs
chromedriver.log

